.TH PLANETFALL 6 "2026-08-31" "planetfall 0.1.0" "Games"
.SH NAME
planetfall \- a translation of Infocom's Planetfall into C
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B planetfall
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B planetfall
is a reimplementation, in ISO C23, of the 1983 Infocom interactive fiction
game
.IR Planetfall ,
written by Steve Meretzky. It is translated from the original ZIL
(Zork Implementation Language) sources rather than interpreted from a
Z-machine story file, so it runs as a native program.
.PP
You play an Ensign Seventh Class aboard the Stellar Patrol Ship
.IR Feinstein .
Commands are typed at the prompt in plain English, in the usual
interactive-fiction style:
.IR "TAKE THE BRUSH" ,
.IR "GO NORTH" ,
.IR "FLOYD, DROP THE BOARD" .
.PP
The translation is incomplete. Consult the project's own notes for what is
and is not yet implemented.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-status
Do not draw the status bar. The game otherwise reserves the top line of the
terminal for it, which is unhelpful when piping input or capturing a
transcript.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Seed the random number generator with
.IR N .
Without this the generator is seeded from the clock, so the explosion delay,
the coolant sequence and the various probability rolls differ between runs.
A fixed seed makes a playthrough reproducible, which is what the test suite
relies on.
.SH COMMANDS
Besides the game's own vocabulary, the following meta-commands are
recognised:
.BR SCORE ,
.BR DIAGNOSE ,
.BR TIME ,
.BR VERBOSE ,
.BR BRIEF ,
.BR SUPERBRIEF ,
.BR SAVE ,
.BR RESTORE ,
.BR SCRIPT ,
.BR UNSCRIPT ,
.BR VERSION ,
.BR AGAIN ,
.BR RESTART
and
.BR QUIT .
None of them consume game time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I planetfall.sav
Saved position, written to the current directory by
.B SAVE
and read back by
.BR RESTORE .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B planetfall
exits 0 when the player quits.
